======================================================================================================================
7.  VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  The field-theory document carries the framework's kernel (nu_RAR) exactly.  The closure program that built and
  killed every relativistic candidate froze a different function, mu_exp(x) = 1 - e^{-x}, and its surviving branch
  then selected mu_10 on Cassini.  SPARC rejects both; mu_10 overwhelmingly.  The ARCHITECTURAL kills are kernel-blind
  by their own certificates and by the identity G = -x^2 mu', so they stand for the framework's kernel too.  The
  kernel-SPECIFIC selection of mu_10 is void.
  The theory of the kernel the data follow exists at the non-relativistic level in closed form (section 5): AQUAL with
  F(X) in polylogarithms, or QUMOND with Q(y) in a dilogarithm; nu_RAR = 1 + Bose-Einstein occupation in sqrt(g_bar a_0).
  It is elliptic and ghost-free in the static sector.  And in that modified-gravity form the Galactic external field
  gives the Solar System a quadrupole of 6.2x (canonical) / 6.8x (alt) the Park 2026 ceiling,
  still 5.8x / 6.3x at g_ext - 1 sigma.  That is Desmond, Hees & Famaey 2024 on this framework's numbers.
  Modified inertia has no such quadrupole (the planets move at accelerations far above a_0 in a field that is not a
  field equation), which is the same side of the fork the disc curl sign (f16-f18) points to -- and modified inertia
  has no local action by Milgrom's theorem and every written completion of it in this repository has failed.
  So: the framework's own kernel has a healthy non-relativistic Lagrangian and that Lagrangian is Cassini-excluded;
  the escape is a theory class with no Lagrangian yet.  The relativistic question has not changed, but the target has:
  it is nu_RAR, not the exponential, and every kernel-specific gate must be re-run on it.

